[[Shauna]] used this spell to fight [[Sophie Casterwill]] upon ambushing the Huntik team with [[Wind]] on their way to a [[Huntik Foundation]] safe house. Shauna was quickly able to knock Sophie to the ground with the spell's help. {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}}

In search of [[Void]], at [[Klaus' bookshop]], Shauna used the spell against [[Stack]]. He was unable to hit Shauna back and was knocked away a big distance by her quick bursts of attacks. {{source|The Blood Spiral}} 

[[Lok Lambert]] and Sophie were tasked to give [[Vigilante]]'s amulet to the [[Huntik Foundation Dutch HQ]]. On their way there, they were ambushed by a pair of Silent Soldiers; the male one used this spell and started fighting Lok. After a struggle, the same Silent Soldier grabbed the knocked female Soldier and fled the encounter. {{source|Den vs Harrison}}

Some Silent Soldiers used the spell to make themselves more agile when going down a mountain to chase the Huntik Team during the mission [[Call of the Casterwill]]. When fighting [[Dante Vale]] during the same mission, at the [[Pyramid of the Sun]], a Silent Soldier used Newfury. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

Harrison Fears used this spell while fighting Lok at the top of the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]], while trying to prevent the Huntik Team from stopping [[Tantras]]' ritual with the [[Heart of Vlad Dracul]]. Harrison was able to knock Lok off the elevated place they were fighting in down through some rooftops. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

New Fury was used again by Shauna to break out of the bonds of a [[Spidertouch]] spell cast by both Dante and [[Den Fears]] during the [[Rise from the Ashes]] mission at the [[Phoenix Volcano]]. {{source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

Shauna used the spell once again on the longest night of the year at the surroundings of the [[Spiral Mark]] against [[Mallory]] and [[White]]. Shauna was quickly able to knock out the two Seekers using the spell's granted extra agility.  {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

At one point, Newfury was used by Shuana against Lok and [[Freelancer]]. {{Source|OAL-089}}

